-- title:
--   Diamond operator on the j=∞ chart as Specσ
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M \ge 1$ with $p \mid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and the hypothesis `hj` that the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` (namely $q^{-1}$ times the integral power series `jNum` read over $\mathbb{Q}$) lies in the level-one $q$-expansion field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the ratios `intFormRatiosC`. Let $\mathfrak P$ be a term of `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, the bundle of properties and pinning data for an integral model `X p (ΓM M H) hj` over the base ring `R p`, let $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and let $\sigma$ be an `R p`-algebra automorphism of the chart algebra `chartAlgInf p (ΓM M H) hj`, i.e. of the subalgebra of elements of `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓM M H)` that are integral over the `R p`-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$, where $j$ is `jAt (ΓM M H) hj`. Assume, as hypothesis `hσ`, that $\sigma$ realises on $q$-expansions the inverse of the diamond automorphism: for every $b$ in the chart algebra, the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (`coeffEmb`) of the $q$-expansion of $\sigma b$ equals the Laurent series underlying the value at the `coeffEmb`-image of $b$ of the inverse of `diamondAutHBar M H d`, the chosen $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` (the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ of the function field of $X_H(M)$) satisfying `IsDiamondAutHBar M H d`, the identity being taken if no such automorphism exists. The conclusion is the equality of morphisms of schemes: the chart morphism `ιInf p (ΓM M H) hj` followed by the morphism underlying $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{dia}\,d$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\sigma$ followed by `ιInf p (ΓM M H) hj`.
--
--   This is the chart-level description of the diamond operator $\langle d \rangle$ on the integral model at $p$: on the $j = \infty$ chart it preserves the chart and acts as the spectrum of the $q$-expansion automorphism $\sigma$ inverse to $\langle d \rangle$ on functions. It is used for the corresponding statement about the diamond operator on the auxiliary level structure and in the analysis of $q$-expansions of functions fixed by the diamond automorphisms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XHDRModelAtP_iotaInf_comp_dia_hom_eq_spec_map_comp_iotaInf.lean

